# Patch files are compared byte-for-byte by `rebuildPatches`, which always writes
# them with LF endings. If a checkout handed them back as CRLF, the first rebuild
# would "regenerate" every patch in the set and the diff would show every file
# changed even though nothing did — so the ending is pinned here rather than left
# to each machine's core.autocrlf.
*.patch text eol=lf
